cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its released artifacts, please cite the
  repository release below and the accompanying preprint once its arXiv
  identifier is assigned (it will be added here).
title: "Microfluidic Native Physics: code and artifacts of 'When Can a Learned Design Surrogate Be Trusted in a Self-Driving Microfluidics Laboratory?'"
type: software
version: "0.5.5-preprint"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Zhiyuan
repository-code: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
url: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocols, deviation registers, number ledger, hash manifests
  and summary artifacts of an offline closed-loop framework for learned
  design surrogates in self-driving microfluidics, built and tested on six
  public tables: sealed validations under chemistry, laboratory and
  cross-table shift, a frozen physics-guided constrained regressor, a
  method-matrix benchmark, pre-registered multi-table hypothesis tests,
  constructive adaptation experiments and a replayed closed-loop benchmark.
  Most pre-registered results are negative; no wet-lab feasibility is claimed.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - microfluidics
  - droplet generation
  - machine learning
  - distribution shift
  - physics-guided regression
  - applicability domain
  - conformal prediction
  - reproducibility
  - self-driving laboratory
  - closed-loop benchmark
